  "description": "YUJMID crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I -4 c 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C123 H124 Gd1 Ni12 O42 S12 2+,2(C4 H9 1+),H2 O1,2(H1),C1 4-. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 10 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni5 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni6 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni7 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni8 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni9 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni10 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni11 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni12 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 21 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.097-3.724 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.62-124.42°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula GdNi12C132S12O47H150.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
